  "default_query_threshold": 100,
  "threshold_rationale": "Measured 2026-08-18 against the June Guntur snapshot, two independent ways. (1) DISCOVERY SATURATION: replaying the 50-query Maps scrape, all 34 clinics were found by query 24; queries 25-50 discovered zero new clinics. Re-run across 40 random query orderings, even the worst order reached 32/34 by query 30 — so discovery alone needs only ~30 queries and is NOT the binding constraint. (2) PHRASING BREADTH: Google autocomplete offers 108 distinct city-qualified phrasings across 28 seeds (mean 4.4 per seed). The score is a visibility MEASUREMENT across the query set, not a discovery exercise: vulnerability's demand term counts how many of N searches a clinic appears in, so resolution depends on phrasing coverage long after every clinic has been found. 14 conditions + 7 treatments asked ~4 ways each gives a floor of ~88; +15% headroom rounds to 100. Also note autocomplete coverage is uneven — acne, eczema, scar and keloid queries return ZERO city-qualified suggestions for Guntur, so those phrasings must come from templates rather than discovery. Caveat: the saturation half is market-size dependent (Guntur has 34 clinics); a larger metro pushes the discovery curve out, while the phrasing floor stays roughly constant.",
  "threshold_evidence": {
    "measured_on": "2026-08-18",
    "source_snapshot": "guntur-ap_dermatology_both_2026-06-28",
    "clinics_total": 34,
    "queries_to_100pct_discovery": 24,
    "new_clinics_per_query_at_50": 0.0,
    "worst_random_order_at_30_queries": 32,
    "distinct_city_qualified_phrasings": 108,
    "mean_suggestions_per_seed": 4.39,
    "phrasing_floor": 88
  }
